.Dd August 1, 2026
.Dt INTEGRIS 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm integris
.Nd high-integrity filesystem sync and backup system (overview)
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm Integris
is a privilege-separated sync and backup system intended to replicate
explicitly authorized filesystem archives between mutually authenticated
nodes on macOS,
.Fx ,
Linux, and
.Ox .
Protected properties include archive identity, containment, authenticity,
integrity, deterministic planning, recoverability, and truthful completion.
.Pp
This manual page describes the installed engineering baseline and how the
shipped tools relate to the future product daemon.
It is not a certification or production-readiness claim.
See
.Xr integrisd 8
for the intended daemon surface.
.Ss Components
.Bl -tag -width "integris-release-digest"
.It Xr integris 1
Local engineering CLI; unidirectional directory sync increment.
.It Xr integris-assure 1
Validate assurance records and the traceability matrix.
.It Xr integris-crash-stub 1
Unix engineering crash harness for publish and journal labels.
.It Xr integris-evidence 1
Run kernel test campaigns and write evidence manifests.
.It Xr integris-release-digest 1
Write an engineering input-digest manifest (not release acceptance).
.It Xr integris-role-stub 1
Unix engineering IPC child for confinement and authority probes.
.It Xr integris-verify-config 1
Validate a configuration document without side effects.
.It Xr integrisd 8
Intended privilege-separated sync and backup daemon
(not yet released as a product binary).
.El
.Ss Installation layout
Portable installs from this repository default to:
.Bl -column ".Pa ${PREFIX}/share/man/man8" "contents" -offset indent
.It Sy directory Ta Sy contents
.It Pa ${PREFIX}/bin Ta command binaries
.It Pa ${PREFIX}/share/man/man1 Ta section 1 pages
.It Pa ${PREFIX}/share/man/man7 Ta this overview
.It Pa ${PREFIX}/share/man/man8 Ta daemon page (integrisd)
.El
.Pp
Traditional BSD ports layouts that use
.Pa ${PREFIX}/man
instead of
.Pa ${PREFIX}/share/man
are selected at install time with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make MANDIR=${PREFIX}/man install-man
.Ed
.Pp
Typical
.Ev PREFIX
values include
.Pa /usr/local
on
.Fx ,
.Ox ,
and many Linux packages;
.Pa /opt/homebrew
or
.Pa /usr/local
on macOS; and
.Pa /usr
for FHS distribution packages.
Destinations respect
.Ev DESTDIR
for staged packaging.
.Ss Assurance model
Every significant decision is expected to have a requirement, rationale,
risk analysis, verifiable specification, verification method, produced
evidence, and named approval role.
On every declared platform, qualifying stable native operating-system and
filesystem facilities must be preferred (requirement INT-IC4-0001);
portable lowest-common-denominator paths are degraded mode only.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
No environment variables are defined by this overview page.
Individual tools document their own variables.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "assurance/requirements.json" -compact
.It Pa assurance/*.json
Normative assurance records.
.It Pa docs/
Specifications, IPs, and policies.
.It Pa evidence/
Campaign manifests and digests.
.It Pa man/
mdoc manual page sources installed by
.Nm make install-man .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Individual tools document their own exit statuses.
As a project convention:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Operational or validation failure.
.It 2
Usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make PREFIX=/usr/local install
make PREFIX=/usr/local MANDIR=/usr/local/man install-man
man integris
man 8 integrisd
.Ed
