.Sh STANDARDS
Normative MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD, and MAY in Integris specifications follow
RFC 2119 and RFC 8174 when capitalized.
.Sh HISTORY
The Integris engineering baseline and these manual pages were introduced
during the M0 to M1 transition.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Integris contributors
.Sh CAVEATS
Integris is not a usable production sync or backup daemon, is not certified,
and makes no SIL or standards-conformance claim.
Product kernels under
.Pa internal/
are reference implementations gated by draft IPs and incomplete IC-1 evidence.
Third-party names such as macOS,
.Fx ,
Linux,
.Ox ,
and Go identify platforms and tools only; see
.Pa TRADEMARKS.md .
